# Environment variables
# ============================================================================
#  You do not need this file to run the portfolio.
#
#  Clone, `npm install`, `npm run dev`. With no configuration at all the app
#  starts an embedded PGlite Postgres in the same process, so every page and
#  the whole motion lab work immediately.
#
#  Copy to `.env.local` only if you want to change something below.
# ============================================================================


# --- Database (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if you want data to survive a restart or a redeploy. Any hosted
# Postgres works: Neon, Vercel Postgres, Supabase, RDS. Postgres 14+.
#
# Use the pooled (-pooler) host with the Neon serverless driver.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require
#
# POSTGRES_URL is used automatically when DATABASE_URL is unset, because that
# is the variable the Vercel Postgres and Neon marketplace integrations create.
# If you installed one of those, you do not need to set anything by hand.
#
# The app deliberately refuses to start in production without a connection
# string rather than falling back to the embedded database, which would lose
# every saved spec on the next cold start.


# --- Database schema (optional) ----------------------------------------------
# Which Postgres schema to put the tables in. Defaults to `public`.
#
# Set this when you share one database with another application so the tables
# are namespaced instead of colliding. Must be a bare identifier: lowercase
# letters, digits and underscores only, not starting with a digit. Anything
# else is rejected at startup rather than interpolated into SQL.
# DATABASE_SCHEMA=portfolio


# --- Contact form (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# Without a key the contact form still validates correctly, then tells the
# visitor that email delivery is not configured and offers a `mailto:` link.
# It never pretends to have sent a message.
#
# With a key it sends real email through Resend. Grab one at resend.com.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# The verified sender address. Use your own domain, or Resend's onboarding
# address while you are testing.
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Portfolio <hello@yourdomain.com>


# --- The public URL ----------------------------------------------------------
# There is no variable for this on purpose. Set `seo.siteUrl` in
# src/config/portfolio.ts instead, because that value also produces the
# OpenGraph tags, the canonical URLs, the sitemap and robots.txt. Keeping it
# next to the rest of your content means one file to edit.
